  "$comment": "Curated concept map for find_tags (scope place) and the geo_lift baseline (PLAN §4.3, §5.3 S6, §11.1; PROBE_FINDINGS G6, G10, G14, C1, C1b). 18 place types. Names, query strings and public taxonomy URNs only (D29). Only taxonomy tags (urn:tag:genre:*, urn:tag:category:*) act as signals; descriptive *:qloo:* tags gave flat or empty results, so none appear here. status: verified = exercised live by the named probe gate; research = named as working during research, not re-checked by a gate; unverified = a candidate URN that must be verified live before it is served. verified_as records the use the probe exercised: heatmap_signal (G6, the restaurant baseline heatmap; P5 and C1, concept heatmaps in Nashville with tag_affinity on every cell) or place_filter (G10, C1 and C1b, a filter-only places call in a metro where every returned place carries the tag). P5 found that only urn:tag:genre:place:* tags shape a heatmap: a urn:tag:category:place:* tag returned no cells, so category tags serve the supply filter only and geo_lift takes heatmap_signal tags as concept_tags. The coverage probe (C1) verified a genre tag for every type. For bookstore and pizza the first category tag the search returned gave 0 Nashville places; C1b verified their other candidates (book_store, pizza_restaurant) as place filters in two map cities. A category tag that is not verified names the gate's fallback (fallback semantic_tag_search, PLAN §11.2): find_tags serves the verified genre tag and looks up a supply filter live, labelled as found at run time, but geo_lift counts similar venues only with a verified place_filter tag, so without one the competitor count is unknown, never 0. fitness_studio is verified through its yoga studio tags. find_tags serves verified and research tags at zero cost and looks up unverified concepts live with semantic_query (/v2/tags, filter.parents.types=urn:entity:place) until a probe verifies them.",
